# nalam.me project context

Personal site of Nazmul Alam, senior software engineer. Static, client-rendered,
served by GitHub Pages from the repo root at `nalam.me`.

## Stack

- **Vite 8** multi-page build, **React 19**, **TypeScript** (strict)
- **Tailwind v4**, CSS-first — there is no `tailwind.config.js`
- **Self-hosted variable fonts**: Newsreader, Geist Sans, Geist Mono
- **shadcn/ui** primitives in `src/components/ui/`
- **Yarn 4** — npm is blocked (`engines.npm: please-use-yarn`)

## The one structural fact to hold onto

**The repo root contains both build output and static assets; all source is in `src/`.**

Generated at the root, never hand-edited: `index.html`, `404.html`, `work/*/index.html`,
`assets/`. If you find yourself editing one of those, you are in the wrong file — edit
`src/` and rebuild.

`build.outDir` is the repo root with **`emptyOutDir: false`**. That flag is load-bearing:
without it a build would delete `CNAME`, `img/`, `docs/` and the entire source tree.
Vite warns about this arrangement on every build; the warning is expected.

## Key files

| File | Role |
|------|------|
| `src/content/site.ts` | **All copy.** Bio, experience, case studies. Components hold no prose. |
| `src/components/Home.tsx` | Home page sections |
| `src/components/CaseStudyPage.tsx` | Shared case study template, selected by slug |
| `src/components/Layout.tsx` | `Page`, `Header`, `Footer`, `Section` |
| `src/styles/globals.css` | Design tokens, base layer, `prose-editorial` |
| `vite.config.ts` | Route registry (`rollupOptions.input`), outDir rules |
| `CONTEXT.md` | Domain vocabulary — use these terms |
| `docs/adr/` | Why the architecture is the way it is |

## Principles

- **Zero third-party requests.** No analytics, no CDN, no remote fonts. Typefaces are
  self-hosted in `src/public/fonts/`. This is a deliberate constraint (ADR-0004), not an
  oversight. Do not add any.
- **The look is deliberately not shadcn-default** — radius 0, cool neutrals, teal accent,
  a three-face type system. See `.cursor/rules/styling.mdc` before changing visuals.
- **Colour values are verified.** `yarn check:contrast` enforces WCAG AA and sRGB gamut.
- **Never publish `docs/resume/`.** Gitignored; contains the CV and a phone number.
- Use Yarn, not npm.
- Prefer editing `src/content/site.ts` over touching components when the change is copy.
- Read `AGENTS.md` and `README.md` before structural changes.
